  "info": {
    "name": "Malabarese ",
    "description": "<td valign=\"top\" width=\"450\">\n<h3> Description:</h3>\r\nIndid-Veddid influenced type of Southwestern India, found in its most typical form in Kerala, e.g. in Malabarese and related people. Common with a large population. It is similar to the Indo Melanids further East, often mixed with Keralids and sometimes with Malids. In Southwestern Dekkan, there exists a more brachimorph variety, the Canarese.\r\n<h3> Physical Traits:</h3>\r\nDark brown skin, black, often wavy hair. Medium height, mesoskelic, ectomorph. Small-headed, dolichocephalic, orthocranic or mildly hypsicranic. Mesorrhine nose, significantly wider than in Indids. The face is short with a mildly prominent chin and full lips. The features overall are less robust and more slender than in the Melanids farther east.<br/>\n<h3> Literature:</h3>\r\nBiasutti described this type together with its Canarese subvariety and grouped them into Paleo Indid together with Tamils (<a href=\"http://humanphenotypes.net/links.html#B67\" target=\"_blank\">Biasutti, 1967)</a>. Eickstedt (<a href=\"http://humanphenotypes.net/links.html#E29\" target=\"_blank\">1929</a>,<a href=\"http://humanphenotypes.net/links.html#E34\" target=\"_blank\">1934</a>,<a href=\"http://humanphenotypes.net/links.html#E37\" target=\"_blank\">1937</a>)  considered it an Indid-Veddoid blend.\r\n\n</td>"
  },
